{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-200713-r4630328","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Spicy Crab Cakes","sourcePageId":200713,"sourceRevision":"4630328","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T21:20:40Z","sourceRevisionUser":"AdoniTzedek","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Spicy%20Crab%20Cakes&oldid=4630328","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:42.816Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Appetizer recipes","Category:Deep fried recipes","Category:Halal recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Pescatarian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for fritters","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using Dijon mustard","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using chipotle chile","Category:Recipes using crab","Category:Recipes using dill","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using mayonnaise","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"a72cf951e7e1ffa3ee90d954203aadeb8af05cd19499963847e87caa958d574f","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Fritter recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThese '''spicy crab cakes''' get an extra kick from cayenne pepper.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Chipotle remoulade ===\n\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Mayonnaise|mayonnaise]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Dijon Mustard|Dijon mustard]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Dill|dill]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 2 tbsp flat-leaf [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]], finely chopped\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Chipotle Pepper|chipotle]] in adobo sauce, [[Cookbook:Puréeing|puréed]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n* Freshly-ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]] to taste\n\n=== Crab cakes ===\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] lump blue [[Cookbook:Crab|crab]] meat\n\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Old Bay|Old Bay]] seasoning\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne]] pepper\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] kosher [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1½ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Dijon Mustard|Dijon mustard]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Mayonnaise|mayonnaise]]\n* Juice of 2 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemons]]\n* [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]] for [[Cookbook:Deep Fat Frying|deep frying]]\n* Panko [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|breadcrumbs]] as needed\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], beaten\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Chipotle remoulade ===\n#Combine all ingredients in a small bowl.\n=== Crab cakes ===\n#Combine all ingredients except for oil, panko, and egg. Shape into 4 equal patties.\n#Dip into egg then dredge in panko. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] at 375°F just until heated through and golden brown.\n#Serve with chipotle remoulade sauce.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using crab]]\n[[Category:Deep fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Appetizer recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fritters]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chipotle chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dill]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon 